                "\n"
                "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n"
                "\n"
                "2. The S.M.A.R.T. Diagnosis (the drives' self-diagnosis)\n"
                "\n"
                "❓ What is it for, exactly?\n"
                "\n"
                "All modern hard drives and SSDs include an internal monitoring system called S.M.A.R.T. (Self-Monitoring, Analysis, and Reporting Technology). It is a bit like a \"black box\" or a permanent doctor that continuously analyzes the internal health of the component: number of start-ups, defective spare sectors, read/write errors, and operating temperature.\n"
                "\n"
                "⚙️ What happens when you start the analysis?\n"
                "\n"
                "The tool directly queries the drive's chips to extract these vital indicators and display them in a clear table (drive model, type, overall OK health status, cumulative power-on hours and live temperature).\n"
